                <pb facs="0319" n="227" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg227"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/9873</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-06T23:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 6, 1918, 11 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 7, 3.10 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3818. Department’s 3830, May 3, 4 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d163-f1"/> In
                    bringing this matter to the attention of the Foreign Office today, Mr. Pichon said that it was his personal opinion
                    that such a declaration as to both Turkey and Bulgaria would be of much help to
                    the Allies. He, however, wishes to bring the question before the Council of the
                    Ministers tomorrow for their consideration before undertaking to answer for the
                    French Government. As soon as I hear further from him I will telegraph his
                    answer.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
